"""Best known packings of N equal circles in a semicircle, N = 100..250: Packomania's table
(https://www.packomania.com/csc/csc.html, complete for N = 1-250, last updated 09 Sep 2026; started by D. A.
Paterson, 2009, with packings by D. W. Cantrell, E. Specht and C. O. Lopez Soto, 2009-2011, and S. Hogan, 2026). The
semicircle has radius 1, its centre at the origin and its diameter on the x axis: y >= 0, x^2 + y^2 <= 1. RADIUS is
the published circle radius (30 digits; 12 digits for N = 146, 157, 159, 176, 177, 194, 195, 202, 205, 244, improved
by S. Hogan on 09 Sep 2026), COORDS the published centres (txt/csc_coords.tar.gz, 30 digits) rounded to binary64, as
base64 of little-endian x y pairs, one string per N; they reproduce RADIUS to 3e-15 relative. The coordinate files
of N = 146, 157, 159, 176, 177, 194, 195, 202, 205, 244 are empty on the site (0 bytes in the archive and in
txt/cscN.txt, 30 Oct 2026), so their centres were read from the published drawings (pdf/cscN.pdf, about 4e-6
precision) and re-maximized on their contacts until the radius matched the published 12-digit one, to 8e-12
relative: they are the published packings rebuilt, not improved."""

